From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:04:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] A subset of CSS: stylesheets, simple selectors and the
 properties Links can render

Links ignored CSS entirely, so pages that lay out their tables with it
(distrowatch.com: every width, vertical-align and colour is in news.css)
came out with side columns centred vertically, ragged columns and
collapsed menus shown expanded.  css.c reads the stylesheets of a
document in order (<style>, <link rel="stylesheet">, @import, @media with
the media type and min-/max-width against the window) and style=""
attributes, and matches rules with type, .class, #id and * compounds
joined by descendant and child combinators (ancestors from the HTML
stack; :link/:visited match, other pseudo-classes, attribute selectors
and the sibling combinators drop the rule), with specificity, order and
!important.  The result is mapped onto what Links renders:

- width, height, vertical-align, text-align, background(-color): answered
  as the attributes width, height, valign, align and bgcolor by
  get_attr_val(), so the table code and the block elements see them and
  the CSS value wins over the HTML attribute;
- color, font-weight, font-style, text-decoration, font-family monospace:
  applied to the element's text format after its handler, and to a table
  cell's contents through css_cell_attr in format_html_part();
- display: none: hides the element like an inline style="display:none".  A hidden block no longer
  breaks the line it would have started (before, a hidden <div> inside
  a list item still put the item's text on two lines);
- display: inline/inline-block, or float, on <li>, <div>, <p>, <ul>, <ol>:
  laid out inline, without the line break and the bullet (horizontal
  menus made of list items); text-align on <ul>/<ol> aligns the list.
- width on form controls, counted in cells of the fixed font links draws
  them in: the size of a text field, the width of a select (its label is
  cut), and a button padded to it.  Button labels no longer break at
  their spaces, and a text field shows its value from the start (the
  cursor used to start at the end, showing the tail of a long value).

External stylesheets are additional files of the document: one that is
not loaded yet sets need_reparse, and the document is formatted again
when it arrives.  The state lives for one really_format_html() call.
There is no box model (margins, padding, borders, float, position, flex).
